Requirements: 12   with obligations: 12

[task-01] The review asks a model, for each defect and each candidate test, whether the
    test would catch the defect. A defect counts as covered as soon as one test is
    recorded as catching it, so once that has happened, asking about the defect's
    remaining tests cannot change how the defect is rated. The review should stop paying
    for those questions.
    -> defect-test-catch-judgment  [functional/explicit]
       For each defect and each candidate test, determine whether the test would catch
       the defect.
    -> defect-covered-on-first-catching-test  [invariant/explicit]
       A defect is counted as covered as soon as one test is recorded as catching it.
    -> stop-paying-for-covered-defect-questions  [functional/explicit]
       Stop asking about a defect's remaining candidate tests once one test has already
       been recorded as catching that defect.

[task-02] Before asking, the review ranks each defect's candidate tests by how similar
    the test's source is to the defect's description, using embeddings. It then asks
    about a defect's tests in that ranked order, in groups sized to the way questions
    are already batched, and stops asking about a defect once the configured number of
    its tests have been recorded as catching it. That number defaults to one.
    -> rank-candidate-tests-by-embedding-similarity  [functional/explicit]
       Rank each defect's candidate tests by how similar the test's source is to the
       defect's description, using embeddings.
    -> rank-defect-tests-by-similarity-order  [functional/explicit]
       Ask about a defect's tests in the ranked order determined by similarity between
       each test's source and the defect's description.
    -> batched-question-groups  [functional/explicit]
       Ask about a defect's tests in groups sized to the way questions are already
       batched.
    -> stop-asking-after-configured-number-of-catching-tests  [functional/explicit]
       Stop asking about a defect once the configured number of its tests have been
       recorded as catching it.
    -> default-catching-tests-count-to-one  [functional/explicit]
       The configured number of tests recorded as catching a defect defaults to one.

[task-03] A defect none of whose tests is recorded as catching it has every one of its
    tests asked about.
    -> test-every-test-asked-about  [functional/explicit]
       A defect none of whose tests is recorded as catching it has every one of its
       tests asked about.

[task-04] A pair the review stops before asking about is not answered. The review
    records it as unjudged, with a cause naming the pair's rank and the tests that had
    already covered the defect. Such a pair never counts toward a defect's unknown
    pairs, and it cannot move how the defect is rated in either direction. That cause
    can only exist on a defect that already has the configured number of catching tests.
    -> unasked-pair-not-answered  [functional/explicit]
       A pair the review stops before asking about is not answered.
    -> unjudged-recorded  [functional/explicit]
       The review records it as unjudged.
    -> cause-names-rank-and-tests  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Record the cause with the pair's rank and the tests that had already covered the
       defect.
    -> unknown-pairs-exclusion  [invariant/explicit]
       A pair the review stops before asking about does not count toward a defect's
       unknown pairs.
    -> defect-rating-unchanged  [invariant/explicit]
       The defect's rating is not changed in either direction by this cause.
    -> cause-only-on-defects-with-configured-catching-tests  [invariant/explicit]
       The cause exists only on a defect that already has the configured number of
       catching tests.

[task-05] The report says, for each defect, how many of its pairs were asked about and
    how many were skipped by stopping early.
    -> pairs-asked-about-count-per-defect  [functional/explicit]
       For each defect, report how many of its pairs were asked about.
    -> skipped-by-stopping-early-count  [functional/explicit]
       The report states how many pairs were skipped by stopping early for each defect.

[task-06] Ranking and stopping can be turned off, so a review can still be run the way
    it runs today.
    -> ranking-and-stopping-can-be-turned-off  [functional/explicit]
       Ranking and stopping can be turned off.
    -> review-can-still-run-as-today  [compatibility/explicit]
       A review can still be run the way it runs today.

[constraint-01] The embedding calls are recorded and replayed like every other model
    call, so two runs over the same input produce identical results.
    -> deterministic-embedding-replay  [compatibility/explicit]
       The embedding calls are recorded and replayed like every other model call, so two
       runs over the same input produce identical results.

[constraint-02] The question put to the model does not change. Nothing about the
    ranking, a test's rank, or whether other tests have already caught the defect
    reaches the model.
    -> question-input-unchanged  [invariant/explicit]
       The question put to the model remains unchanged.
    -> ranking-not-exposed-to-model  [invariant/explicit]
       The model is not given ranking information.
    -> test-rank-not-exposed-to-model  [invariant/explicit]
       The model is not given a test's rank.
    -> prior-catches-not-exposed-to-model  [invariant/explicit]
       The model is not given whether other tests have already caught the defect.

[constraint-03] This works on whatever pairs are left after the review has already set
    pairs aside for other reasons, such as what the project's tests did under an
    injected edit.
    -> leftover-pairs-only  [functional/explicit]
       Apply this step only to whatever pairs remain after the review has already set
       pairs aside for other reasons, including pairs skipped because the project's
       tests under an injected edit already handled them.

[exclusion-01] Changing what is sent in an embedding request.
    -> embedding-request-unchanged  [docs_config/explicit]
       The change does not alter what is sent in an embedding request.

[exclusion-02] Skipping pairs of a defect that no test has caught, by rank or by any
    other cheaper check.
    -> skip-uncaught-pairs-by-rank-or-cheaper-check  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not skip pairs of a defect that no test has caught, whether by
       rank or by any other cheaper check.

[exclusion-03] Changing which tests are candidates for a defect.
    -> preserve-candidate-test-set  [invariant/explicit]
       The change does not alter which tests are candidates for a defect.

